      "hints": [
        "Set $2\\sin^2\\theta - 1 = \\frac{1}{4} \\implies \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{5}{8}$.",
        "In fourth quadrant, $\\sin\\theta = -\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{8}} \\approx -0.7906$.",
        "Solve $\\theta = -52.2^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the result from part (a)(i) into the equation:\n$$2\\sin^2\\theta - 1 = \\frac{1}{4} \\implies 2\\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{5}{4} \\implies \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{5}{8}$$",
        "Take the negative square root since $-90^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 0^\\circ$ (where sine is negative):\n$$\\sin\\theta = -\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{8}} \\approx -0.7906$$",
        "Find $\\theta$ to 1 decimal place:\n$$\\theta = -\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{8}}\\right) \\approx -52.24^\\circ \\approx -52.2^\\circ$$"
      ],
